{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1511766-artifacts-how-do-they-work","id":1511766,"title":"Artifacts - How do they work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-15T20:40:10-07:00","id":1511766,"title":"Artifacts - How do they work?","content":"Trinity Continuum Core Pg 91 shows a chart that gives the following:<br /> <br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1238_1684199988605_782\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1238\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1238\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1238&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b<br /> But on Pg 93 it states:<br /> <br /> &quot;The chart below lists the item\u2019s maximums by Rank.<br /> <b>Maximum Enhancement</b>: This is the highest<br /> Enhancement the item may provide on related<br /> actions.<br /> <b>Maximum Edge Dots:</b> This is the most dots<br /> worth of Edges (or number of Gifts/Psi dots) the<br /> item can mimic.<br /> <b>Maximum Tags:</b> This is the maximum number of<br /> Tags the item may possess if it is a weapon, armor,<br /> or vehicle.<br /> <br /> Rank 1 and Rank 2 devices may have both their maximum number of Enhancements and Edges without increasing the item\u2019s Rank.<br /> <b>When crafting items of Rank 3 and above</b>,<u> the player should choose between the maximum number of Enhancements or Edges</u>.<br /> The Story guide may allow a combination of both, though <b>the total number of dots shouldn\u2019t exceed the Enhancement rating for that Rank</b>.&quot;\u200b<br /> <br /> So the chart really messes me up, because the maximum enhancement is 6, but the maximum edge (and gifts) dots is 10.<br /> Is the chart wrong? Is the paragraph? Which do I use?<br /> <br /> If I make or acquire a 5th rank artifact, will it give me a +6 enhancement on specific actions, access to 10 gifts/edges, and 5 tags if it's a cool weapon/arm?<br /> Or does it give me a +6 enhancement on specific actions OR 6 dots in gifts and 5 tags if its a weapon/armor?<br /> <br /> If not, can someone do a better job of explaining what the hard rules for this are? Fluff need not apply just yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25261-solarknight","name":"SolarKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T21:33:40-07:00","id":1511771,"title":"","content":"The crafting rules never made much sense. The recent Player's Guide Backerfit project included a stretch goal &quot;<b>THE ART OF CRAFTS</b> \u2013 The unlocked PDF supplement will be expanded to include a streamlined version of the crafting system, along with some examples, to help inventor characters make new toys for their Talents.\u200b&quot; Hopefully that'll finally explain how crafting is supposed to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T10:45:58-07:00","id":1511812,"title":"","content":"My suggestion is in my signature, the House Rules - The Basics.<br /> Last chapter is what you are looking for.<br /> <br /> Shepherdboi is correct, but it will take a few years before this book shows up\u2026 so\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 05-16-2023, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T17:54:04-07:00","id":1511833,"title":"","content":"There are two distinct columns in the charts, one for Max Enhancement and another for the dots of anything else that is available. The statement that you must pick one or the other tells me that if you pick Enhancement, you use that column. If you pick the other, you use it. If you make a hybrid, you use the much lower Enhancement column as a dot limit.<br /> <br /> (The enhancement bonus is so much lower than the other dots, you will probably almost always benefit from figuring out an edge that gives an appropriate Enhancement bonus and give that, instead.)<br /> <br /> <br /> On a related aside: The systems for making armor and weapons don't correlate well with the crafting rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T01:31:16-07:00","id":1513365,"title":"","content":"Wish I could help, but neither the crafting rules nor the equipment rules made the slightest bit of sense to me. In fact, they frustrated me so much that I stopped trying to play trinity continuum altogether. My advice is to get the house rules pdf from Mateus and other similar products in drivethrurpg, at least till we get the new crafting supplement. They're the reason I gave the trinity continuum system another chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}